  "claim": "The New Yorker magazine was started in 1925 and featured the work of the journalist that wrote The Billion-Dollar Molecule.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Barry Werth. Sentence: His work has appeared in \"The New York Times\", \"The New Yorker\", \"GQ\", the \"Smithsonian\", and the \"MIT Technology Review\".\nPage: The New Yorker. Sentence: Started as a weekly in 1925, the magazine is now published 47 times annually, with five of these issues covering two-week spans.\nPage: The Billion-Dollar Molecule. Sentence: The Billion-Dollar Molecule is a book by journalist Barry Werth about the founding and early research efforts of the American biotechnology company Vertex Pharmaceuticals, which was founded in 1989 by Joshua Boger and was among the first biotechnology companies to adopt an explicit strategy of rational drug design as opposed to techniques based on combinatorial chemistry.",
