        "original_id": "2d1cf1b0-94e4-56e3-9af7-13b2cc7cebfd",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Barry Werth, Joshua Boger\n- Organizations: The New Yorker, The New York Times, GQ, Smithsonian, MIT Technology Review, Vertex Pharmaceuticals\n- Products: The Billion-Dollar Molecule\n- Topics: publishing frequency, journalism, biotechnology, rational drug design, combinatorial chemistry\n\nFacts:\n- The New Yorker started as a weekly magazine in 1925.\n- The New Yorker is now published 47 times annually, with five issues covering two-week spans.\n- Barry Werth's work has appeared in The New York Times, The New Yorker, GQ, Smithsonian, and MIT Technology Review.\n- Vertex Pharmaceuticals was founded in 1989 by Joshua Boger.\n- Vertex Pharmaceuticals was among the first biotechnology companies to adopt an explicit strategy of rational drug design instead of techniques based on combinatorial chemistry.\n- The Billion-Dollar Molecule is a book by journalist Barry Werth about the founding and early research efforts of Vertex Pharmaceuticals.",
